<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Shield Capture — Info.plist.

  The important thing about this file is what is NOT in it.

  There is no NSPhotoLibraryUsageDescription and there must never be one. A
  photograph chosen from storage cannot be attested, so the server refuses it;
  a library path in this app would be a control that looks available and always
  fails, which reads as a bug rather than as the decision it is. Without the
  key, iOS itself will not hand this app a library image, so the guarantee does
  not depend on anybody remembering it.

  NSCameraUsageDescription is required — AVCapturePhotoOutput is the only thing
  in the app that produces bytes.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>CFBundleName</key>
  <string>Shield</string>
  <key>CFBundleDisplayName</key>
  <string>Shield Capture</string>

  <key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
  <string>Shield photographs work at the moments it stops being inspectable. A picture chosen from your library cannot prove where it came from, so the camera is the only way in.</string>

  <key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
  <string>Your position is recorded with each photograph and measured against the site the record names. It is treated as a claim by this device, not as proof.</string>

  <!-- DO NOT ADD NSPhotoLibraryUsageDescription. See the comment above. -->
</dict>
</plist>
